  "articleBody": "So, you're getting ready for finish carpentry installation—that's exciting! Knowing what to expect can make the whole process smoother. First off, we'll confirm all the dimensions and opening conditions to make sure everything lines up. It's super important to verify that door frames are plumb and square and that openings are ready for their new trim or doors. Then, the actual installation begins: setting and shimming your doors, frames, or trim pieces precisely. This is where attention to detail really matters for that seamless look. After everything is set, we fasten and align everything carefully, making sure joints are tight and lines are clean. We'll also check all the reveals—those small, consistent gaps—around your doors and ensure everything operates smoothly before moving on. Finally, there's the finish touch-up, which involves filling nail holes and light sanding to prepare for paint or stain, leaving you with a polished look. Sometimes, small jobs can be scheduled within 1-3 weeks, while bigger projects might take 2-6 weeks depending on material availability and our current workload, but we always keep you informed. It’s also crucial to ask about protecting the work area and the cleanup process; we always strive to keep your home tidy. For installations where door function, squareness, and matching existing finishes are critical, a professional touch guarantees a result you'll love. Give us a call at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your project!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
